<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Tool Approval</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top:0; }

    </style>
</head>
<body>
    This is an overview of all tools supplied by the MCP Server "${MCP_SERVER_NAME}".<br>
    It allows you to determine which tools the language model can access.

    <br><br>
    You can manage tool access by enabling or disabling individual tools.<br>
    The status of a tool determines its visibility to the LLM:
    <ul>
        <li>Tools marked as "Approved" will be invoked automatically.</li>
        <li>Tools marked as "Prompted" will be prompted for approval before every invocation.</li>
        <li>Blocked tools will not be visible to the LLM.</li>
    </ul>
</body>
</html>
